    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1184">

                <pb facs="0962" n="846" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg846"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/6946.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Silliman</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Although Belt telegraphed November 20 from Saltillo that General Carranza had
                    ordered proper authorities to station a guard at Los Mochis, Department informed
                    anarchy still prevails there and that properties of about fifty American
                    settlers are being looted. Americans have been driven from their homes and fear
                    total destruction their holdings. United States naval vessel stationed at
                    Topolobampo telegraphed yesterday nothing had been done for relief Los
                    Mochis.</p>
                <p>Urge General Carranza immediately to order an adequate force to garrison Los
                    Mochis permanently, otherwise a repetition of the present conditions is certain
                    to occur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
